      "Directional U-shape test (all of: response vs immediate lower; long-term vs response higher), intersection p = 0.989. Not statistically significant at the 5% level: the data do not reject the null of no U-shape. The point estimates do not have the hypothesised shape: long-term vs response goes the other way.",
      "- response vs immediate: rate ratio 0.95 (95% CI 0.61-1.49), no direction can be read from it; one-sided p = 0.411 (alternative: lower). Not statistically significant at the 5% level: the data do not reject the null of no decrease (rate ratio at least 1); the 95% CI runs from 0.61 to 1.49, which includes 1. Repeat events: 61 in the response period and 28 in the immediate period.",
      "- long-term vs response: rate ratio 0.67 (95% CI 0.47-0.94), no direction can be read from it; one-sided p = 0.989 (alternative: higher). Not statistically significant at the 5% level: the data do not reject the null of no increase (rate ratio at most 1); the 95% CI runs from 0.47 to 0.94. The estimate is in the opposite direction to the hypothesis (lower, not higher). Repeat events: 83 in the long-term period and 61 in the response period.",
      "- long-term vs immediate: rate ratio 0.63 (95% CI 0.41-0.99), about 37% lower; two-sided p = 0.045. Statistically significant at the 5% level: the data reject equal rates (rate ratio 1). Repeat events: 83 in the long-term period and 28 in the immediate period."
    ],
